<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ProvingGround.Pipeline.publish.xml — a copy of the estate pipeline's publish settings, so a
  local proof can reproduce what the real deployment would do.

  Status: placeholder, not yet verified against the pipeline. The estate publishes through
  Azure DevOps -> Octopus, and the DacFx flags are fixed in the pipeline's own XML. This file
  will hold those flags once someone records them from the pipeline (together with the DacFx
  version, pinned in ../../estate/toolchain.md). Until then it uses the production settings the
  Twin corpus already proved: the block and smart-default settings match the Strict profile,
  and the drop setting is the one production actually uses.

    BlockOnPossibleDataLoss = True   -> the locked gate. This pipeline cannot relax it.
    GenerateSmartDefaults   = False  -> the deploy does not backfill missing values on its own.
    DropObjectsNotInSource  = False  -> the production drop setting. Deleting a .sql file drops
                                        nothing: the object and its rows survive the publish (a
                                        "phantom"). A real drop ships as an explicit, ordered
                                        pre-deployment script instead.
    IgnoreColumnOrder       = True   -> a change in column order alone does not count as a change.

  Two profiles, two jobs. This one shows the deployment-shaped outcome, phantoms included. The
  Strict profile makes a would-be drop visible on the disposable copy. Use Strict to find out
  what a change would remove; use this one to see what the pipeline would actually do.

  To turn this file from a placeholder into a verified replica:
    1. Record the pipeline's DacFx publish flags and version in ../../estate/toolchain.md.
    2. Copy the flags into this file exactly. Note any flag that differs from this draft.
    3. Publish once against a disposable copy. Confirm the trust outcome (is_not_trusted = 0
       on a foreign-key add) matches what FINDINGS_AND_CHANGES.md Part 5 expects for that
       DacFx version.
    4. Delete this status note and record the date the verification ran.

  Point this profile only at the ProvingGround database on the warm container, which is a
  disposable copy of Dev. Never point it at a real database. A publish is a publish, whichever
  settings it uses.
-->
<Project ToolsVersion="Current" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetConnectionString>Server=localhost,11433;Initial Catalog=ProvingGround;User ID=sa;Password=Projection@Strong1;TrustServerCertificate=True;Encrypt=False</TargetConnectionString>
    <BlockOnPossibleDataLoss>True</BlockOnPossibleDataLoss>
    <GenerateSmartDefaults>False</GenerateSmartDefaults>
    <IgnoreColumnOrder>True</IgnoreColumnOrder>
    <DropObjectsNotInSource>False</DropObjectsNotInSource>
    <IncludeTransactionalScripts>True</IncludeTransactionalScripts>
    <AllowIncompatiblePlatform>False</AllowIncompatiblePlatform>
    <IgnorePermissions>True</IgnorePermissions>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
